{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the \"150 units in stock for each product by the end of the fourth quarter\" requirement, is this an exact target (inventory must equal exactly 150 for each product at the end of Q4), or is it a minimum (inventory must be at least 150, with any excess allowed)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether the inventory constraint is an exact equality or a minimum threshold."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Regarding the \"contract reservations\" (demand) per quarter per product, is the requirement that each quarter's demand must be fully met from that quarter's production plus beginning inventory (i.e., no backlogging allowed, and any unmet demand incurs the delay compensation cost), or can demand be delayed to later quarters where the delay compensation cost applies?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response presents a single binary choice regarding the policy for meeting demand (immediate fulfillment vs. backlogging), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When a unit of demand is delayed by one quarter, does the delay compensation cost apply only for that single quarter of delay (i.e., a unit delayed by 2 quarters incurs 2 × the per-quarter delay cost), or is it a flat one-time penalty regardless of how many quarters late it is?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding how delay costs are calculated (linear vs. flat), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Regarding the 15,000 production hours per quarter limit, is this a hard upper bound (total hours used in each quarter must be ≤ 15,000), or is it a capacity that can be exceeded at some additional cost (e.g., overtime)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the nature of the production hour limit (hard bound vs. flexible capacity)."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Regarding the inventory holding cost of 5 yuan per unit per quarter, does this apply to all units held in inventory at the end of each quarter (including the 150 units that must be held at the end of Q4), or only to units that were produced in a prior quarter and are being carried forward to meet future demand (i.e., the final 150 units at end of Q4 are exempt from holding cost)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the scope of the inventory holding cost, specifically whether it applies to all ending inventory or excludes the mandatory Q4 ending stock. This is a single binary choice."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Regarding the delay compensation cost, does it apply to units that are delivered late relative to their original quarter, even if they are ultimately delivered before the end of Q4? For example, if a unit of Product I demanded in Q1 is delivered in Q2, does it incur 20 yuan of delay compensation, or does delay compensation only apply to units not delivered by the end of Q4?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the definition and application scope of delay compensation costs, using an example to illustrate the specific scenario in question."
}

